DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddoommaaiinnnnaammee utility prints the name of the current YP/NIS domain.  The
     super-user can set the domain name by supplying an argument; this is usu‐
     ally done with the _n_i_s_d_o_m_a_i_n_n_a_m_e variable in the _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._c_o_n_f file, nor‐
     mally run at boot time.

NNOOTTEESS
     The YP/NIS (formerly ``Yellow Pages'' but renamed for legal reasons) do‐
     main name does not necessarily have anything to do with the Domain Name
     System domain name, although they are often set equal for administrative
     convenience.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     getdomainname(3), rc.conf(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ddoommaaiinnnnaammee command appeared in FreeBSD 1.1, based on a similar com‐
     mand in SunOS.

